      "--stimulus",
      "a note held through the effect on one of this unit's own voices -- program 16, bank nought, sounded at note 81, which arrives at four hundred and forty hertz. Not a signal presented at the analogue input: this unit's input reaches its output and bypasses every one of its effects, which is measured and published beside this. The voice is not a single partial and this reading does not need it to be, because what is read off it is a level: the order it carries most is the third, and the take in this record made with the part routed past the effect says so in its own figures. A limiter is a gain that depends on the level, so every order of a tone through one moves by the same number of decibels; an order here that moves by a different number is a reading about the stage and not about the voice. The part's own volume is what this record sweeps, and nothing inside the type reaches the level going in. Every rung carries a take made with the part routed past the effect, which is what says what the volume did to the carrier before the stage saw it.",
